{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996316-clash-of-wills","id":996316,"title":"Clash Of Wills","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-31T16:20:24-07:00","id":996316,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Clash Of Wills","content":"The mechanics of a Clash of Wills is pretty straight forward. However there is one part of the rules that I'd really like to make sure I understand correctly:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtAw2 pg 118</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages may spend Willpower to bolster the contested roll, and are always aware when their spells are clashing.</div> </div> </div> </div>So by way of example, if a Moros has cast corpse mask on a dead body to change the cause of death, and another Mage comes along and inspects the body with Forensic Gaze, they know immediately that something isn't right, regardless of whether or not they are the successful party in the Clash, because they still know that their spell is clashing with something. Is that right?<br /> <br /> I find myself deeply ambivalent about this rule if that's the case. On the one hand, from a meta perspective I can see the appeal of not ever having an avenue of investigation completely closed off by a potent veiling effect that would otherwise throw a potentially insurmountable roadblock.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it seems to me that a lot of veiling effects would be ruined by being able to immediately discern that something is amiss, even if they party attempting to perceive fails the Clash. Moreover, it would seem that the narrower the parameters of the detection effect, the more likely you are to get the truth of something regardless of the outcome of the Clash.<br /> <br /> I'm tempted to rule that the party attempting to perceive does not get to know their spell is clashing if the effect in question is from the practice of veiling and their attempt fails. Thoughts?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/358-emanantvolition","user":"EmanantVolition","date":".  for clarity 10-31-2016, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/358-emanantvolition","name":"EmanantVolition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T16:32:23-07:00","id":996318,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking about this myself. As you say, there are cases where it seems like having a Clash at all would be most of the information an investigator needs. Like, suppose I create a false history with Veiling for Postcognition purposes- does an investigator clash automatically as soon as they see it? If not, how do they trigger &quot;looking deeper?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T17:23:50-07:00","id":996339,"title":"","content":"Yes, that's right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T17:27:19-07:00","id":996342,"title":"","content":"I'm cautious about this rule for the same reason you are, Volition, but something worth remembering is that awareness of your spell clashing isn't <i>always</i> sufficient to tell you what you want to know. For example, it doesn't tell you what your spell is clashing with or why, and a failure on a clash means you don't gain access to that information.<br /> <br /> Likewise, this rule only applies to spells, which means Mage Sight doesn't get this benefit of being auto-aware of a Clash.<br /> <br /> In other words, a Veiling spell to make you invisible and an Unveiling spell to detect invisible things will Clash, but if the Unveiling spell loses, all they know is that there's someone invisible nearby, not where they are. Likewise, an Obrimos activating their Forces Sight at the Active level gets an auto-Clash but don't learn anything on a failure.<br /> <br /> So while a Moros casting Forensic Gaze and failing a Clash may instantly know <i>something</i> is amiss, they don't know what that something is. They just know this corpse is touched by spellery. They might suspect a casting of Corpse Mask, but what if it's Suppress Life and this is merely a sleeping person? Or even simply a vampire having a snooze with a spell cast on them by a friend to keep anyone from thinking them anything but a properly dead person?<br /> <br /> All this rule does is tell the Mage that there's something amiss. From there, it's up to Focused Mage Sight - which will almost certainly win in a Clash for a modestly experienced Mage - if they think it's worth burning willpower to find out what's beneath.<br /> <br /> In the end, it feels like a good rule to use, to my mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T18:31:10-07:00","id":996381,"title":"","content":"Way I'd handle it is like a good old fashioned mystery, assuming the investigator . You know someone messed with the crime-scene, but you A) don't necessarily know it was done with awakened magic, (barring Prime use) B) don't know what they changed, C) don't know why they changed it.<br /> <br /> You want to scrutinize it again? Sure, muddle it up with some mana. Let's see how much you contaminate it before you get a clear view of what happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T20:03:44-07:00","id":996408,"title":"","content":"For the perception challenge side, I really like this rule. It's harder to metagame when the game rules that the character just knows something's up.<br /> <br /> <i>My</i> ambivalence comes from the automatic knowledge someone looked. I mean, you can theoretically heat map your sanctum using this aspect, knowing not just if someone is present, but <i>where they are looking</i>, if you bother to get that fine about it, simply by casting various small effects.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I love how paranoid an invader would start to get if someone actually did that. He keeps clashing literally everywhere he looks: That painting uses slightly different colors. That figurine is actually rotated a few degrees. Can't see what's going on over there, though. More stupid stuff? Something important? With enough precision, you could simply set off conventional weapons remotely. &quot;Ah, he found the door; I'll set off that mine, now&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> I was curious from the development discussions how Clash and Relinquish were going to interact. Looks like they don't, at least not from what I've seen;only Dispel Magic seems to care if the spell was relinquished. (Even relinquished spells normally reveal clashes but not dispellation? Seems incongruous. Be curious why, if it's intentional.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T20:20:47-07:00","id":996410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996316-clash-of-wills?p=996342#post996342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likewise, this rule only applies to spells, which means Mage Sight doesn't get this benefit of being auto-aware of a Clash.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. I did not notice that it only mentions spells for the auto-aware on a Clash, but honestly I wonder if that isn't reading too much into it. That same sentence also says that a Mage may spend Willpower on the contested roll, and doesn't stipulate that that only occurs on spells. You probably can't spend Willpower on a roll you don't even know you're making in character.<br /> <br /> Awakening 1e had what 2e calls an attainment in Tome of the Mysteries at Prime 2 called Spell Cloak, which occluded spells from Unseen Senses and made them much harder to see with Mage Sight for 1 Mana. It's distinctly missing from 2e Awakening though.<br /> <br /> I think i'll play it with the rules as written for the first few sessions to see how it works out in play before I make decide on making any changes, but I might need to consider bringing Spell Cloak back in as an attainment in 2e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996316-clash-of-wills?p=996342#post996342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They just know this corpse is touched by <b>spellery</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my new favorite word.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/358-emanantvolition","name":"EmanantVolition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T20:55:47-07:00","id":996425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996316-clash-of-wills?p=996408#post996408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the perception challenge side, I really like this rule. It's harder to metagame when the game rules that the character just knows something's up.<br /> <br /> <i>My</i> ambivalence comes from the automatic knowledge someone looked. I mean, you can theoretically heat map your sanctum using this aspect, knowing not just if someone is present, but <i>where they are looking</i>, if you bother to get that fine about it, simply by casting various small effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see where you're coming from here, but for me knowing that your spell has clashed for the &quot;defender&quot; is definitely more feature than bug. For one, heat-mapping your sanctum is limited by Gnosis-derived spell control caps. But mostly, knowing that your spells are clashing doesn't really ruin the intended purpose of the attacking spell the way that information can ruin the intended purpose of a concealing spell.<br /> <br /> For example, if a Mastigos Adept conceals his thoughts with Alter Mental Pattern, and his Mastigos Apprentice tries to casts Know Nature, the odds are pretty high that the reason his spell is clashing is because the Mastigos Adept is altering his thoughts. In fact, if he loses the clash but the spell still successfully returns an &quot;answer&quot;, he knows with a high degree of certainty that this is what's happening, because if this was a straight up defense or concealment, his spell wouldn't &quot;return&quot; anything at all. Knowing and Unveiling spells are already incredibly strong, so I'm having a hard time shaking the feeling that the additional information that being auto-aware on a clash provides with no additional investment on the caster's part just seems too good. My concern is specifically with concealing and revealing effects, though - auto-aware clash on other effects seems much less (potentially) problematic to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/358-emanantvolition","name":"EmanantVolition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T21:22:12-07:00","id":996439,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it, I've a few Clash of Wills related questions I might as well post to this thread.<br /> <br /> 1) In WtF 2E, Clash of Wills for a spirit is Rank + dots of an Influence if appropriate. However, Spirit 5 Annihilate Spirit list the Clash of Wills for a Spirit as Power + Finesse. Is this how mage defines a Spirit's Clash of Wills dicepool? It seems pretty unlikely that a Mage will ever defeat a Spirit of consequence on a Gnosis + Arcanum vs Power + Finesse roll-off.<br /> <br /> 2) If a mage has multiple effects that would cause a Clash of Wills, do they check for each one, or only against the strongest/most relevant? For example, if I've got both Alter Mental Pattern and Supernal Veil in place, and someone attempts to cast Know Nature to glean information from my surface thoughts, do they clash against each spell, or just once against whichever spell has the greater dice pool?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/358-emanantvolition","name":"EmanantVolition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T21:38:07-07:00","id":996442,"title":"","content":"I've asked about the spirit Clash of Wills dicepool before, I'm surprised it isn't mentioned in the book actually. I treat it as Rank+Influence (only if applicable), remember that ephemeral entities can spend Willpower, and just assume that moderately experienced mages usually winning a Clash against ephemerals is a feature not a bug. The higher pool for Annihilate Spirit might be because it's a straight-up save or die effect, I think it's generally too high unless you want ephemerals to be incredibly potent (which you might).<br /> <br /> In the interest of moving things along in a real gameplay situation, I would take a page from Withstand ratings and say that multiple Clash effects means you take the highest applicable dicepool and add +1 for each additional one, and just have that count for all of them. Or if you wanted to get fancy, maybe take the highest applicable dicepool and give it 9-again if there are 2 effects, and 8-again if there are 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T21:59:24-07:00","id":996447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EmanantVolition</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996316-clash-of-wills?p=996410#post996410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. I did not notice that it only mentions spells for the auto-aware on a Clash, but honestly I wonder if that isn't reading too much into it. That same sentence also says that a Mage may spend Willpower on the contested roll, and doesn't stipulate that that only occurs on spells. You probably can't spend Willpower on a roll you don't even know you're making in character.<br /> <br /> Awakening 1e had what 2e calls an attainment in Tome of the Mysteries at Prime 2 called Spell Cloak, which occluded spells from Unseen Senses and made them much harder to see with Mage Sight for 1 Mana. It's distinctly missing from 2e Awakening though.<br /> <br /> I think i'll play it with the rules as written for the first few sessions to see how it works out in play before I make decide on making any changes, but I might need to consider bringing Spell Cloak back in as an attainment in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless specified, you usually cannot spend WP if you're unaware, no.<br /> <br /> As for Spell Cloak, there's no need for the attainment; remember, <i>all</i> concealment spells work automatically against Peripheral Mage Sight without a Clash. Only Active Sight provokes it. A Prime 2 Veiling spell cast either as a Combined spell or by an ally could cover it up pretty easily (with a ruling that, naturally, a spell that veils another spell also veils itself*).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">*Also, any Paradox caused by such a spell summons an Abyssal entity known as The One Who Shaves The Barber.</span><br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EmanantVolition</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996316-clash-of-wills?p=996425#post996425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, if a Mastigos Adept conceals his thoughts with Alter Mental Pattern, and his Mastigos Apprentice tries to casts Know Nature, the odds are pretty high that the reason his spell is clashing is because the Mastigos Adept is altering his thoughts. In fact, if he loses the clash but the spell still successfully returns an &quot;answer&quot;, he knows with a high degree of certainty that this is what's happening, because if this was a straight up defense or concealment, his spell wouldn't &quot;return&quot; anything at all. Knowing and Unveiling spells are already incredibly strong, so I'm having a hard time shaking the feeling that the additional information that being auto-aware on a clash provides with no additional investment on the caster's part just seems too good. My concern is specifically with concealing and revealing effects, though - auto-aware clash on other effects seems much less (potentially) problematic to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:12px\">This doesn't really ruin the intent of the defending spell, though. The Apprentice doesn't know if the Clash is caused by Alter Mental Pattern, or Mental Shield, or a Counterspell, or a Goetic demon surfacing or the Adept carrying a coin of thaumium... The list goes on. There is a huge list of reasons a spell might go pop off of someone.<br /> <br /> The rules aren't really clear whether he knows he wins the Clash or not. Presumably, all the Mage senses is that he gets an answer. It could be true, it could be false. Such is the paranoid world the Awakened live in.<br /> <br /> And even <i>if</i> they get the information back, do they know what patterns are being changed? By whom? To what end?<br /> <br /> So much information is not revealed still. Remember, all it says is that a Mage knows when their spells are clashing. It doesn't say they know the outcomes beyond what their other senses may tell them.</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2855,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","user":"Axelgear","date":". 11-01-2016, 01:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T22:36:45-07:00","id":996458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EmanantVolition</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996316-clash-of-wills?p=996425#post996425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For one, heat-mapping your sanctum is limited by Gnosis-derived spell control caps.</div> </div> </div> </div>For that to be true, there would need to be a limit on Clashes of Will to those things that are governed by your spell control limit. If you don't mind spending the willpower to relinquish, you don't have to limit yourself to that limit. That <i>is</i> why I brought up relinquishment. If you use temp WP, you'd need to worry with recovering the will, finding the time, and dispelling the array before things go awry, but otherwise, you could theoretically get highly refined eye-tracking against anyone not using Space.<br /> <br /> Of course that is a silly example, since keeping track of all of that is something that shouldn't be easy or even possible, but it does seem to indicate that a mage knows that a spell clashed and which one.<br /> <br /> Some mechanic like Withstand when you relinquish could work, if you wanted to implement it. Maybe just leave a die penalty. Either of those would, however, fly in the obvious design mechanic of &quot;Don't store state about spells beyond the active factors&quot;. Dunno. I'd like to play the system a bit before deciding, myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T07:50:21-07:00","id":996587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996316-clash-of-wills?p=996458#post996458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For that to be true, there would need to be a limit on Clashes of Will to those things that are governed by your spell control limit. If you don't mind spending the willpower to relinquish, you don't have to limit yourself to that limit. That <i>is</i> why I brought up relinquishment. If you use temp WP, you'd need to worry with recovering the will, finding the time, and dispelling the array before things go awry, but otherwise, you could theoretically get highly refined eye-tracking against anyone not using Space.<br /> <br /> Of course that is a silly example, since keeping track of all of that is something that shouldn't be easy or even possible, but it does seem to indicate that a mage knows that a spell clashed and which one.<br /> <br /> Some mechanic like Withstand when you relinquish could work, if you wanted to implement it. Maybe just leave a die penalty. Either of those would, however, fly in the obvious design mechanic of &quot;Don't store state about spells beyond the active factors&quot;. Dunno. I'd like to play the system a bit before deciding, myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWhy would relinquished spells ping the Mage that relinquished them when they clash? If you've relinquished a spell, it isn't 'yours' anymore, and so I don't see why you'd have any awareness of what was happening to it. I certainly don't see why you'd get to spend Willpower to bolster it if it's not in one of your spell control slots. You'd still use the Clash rules, because it keeps the mechanics tidy, but you shouldn't get the additional built in advantages. And especially because those advantages are unique to mages anyway, they're not intrinsic to the Clash rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":614,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","user":"Eolirin","date":". 11-01-2016, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T18:50:57-07:00","id":996931,"title":"","content":"Considering a clash makes it seem like something's off anyway...<br /> Why not have a character use that to their advantage?<br /> <br /> Like they go to veil the corpse, but they don't change anything about how it's perceived at all,<br /> then someone comes in and notices a clash but fails and gets all paranoid about the false positive.<br /> &quot;What am I not seeing about this corpse?!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T19:41:33-07:00","id":996953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eolirin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996316-clash-of-wills?p=996587#post996587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bWhy would relinquished spells ping the Mage that relinquished them when they clash? If you've relinquished a spell, it isn't 'yours' anymore, and so I don't see why you'd have any awareness of what was happening to it. I certainly don't see why you'd get to spend Willpower to bolster it if it's not in one of your spell control slots. You'd still use the Clash rules, because it keeps the mechanics tidy, but you shouldn't get the additional built in advantages. And especially because those advantages are unique to mages anyway, they're not intrinsic to the Clash rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only line supporting that which I have found is under Relinquishment : (MtAw2E pg118) &quot;The player can spend a Willpower point to leave the spell as though cast by another mage.&quot;<br /> This is enough to make a good argument, but it's far from compelling or clear-cut.<br /> Why should the mage be allowed a Clash for another mage's spell, at all? That raises weird questions, too.<br /> <br /> <br /> It <i>looks</i> like Relinquished spells were going to have a Withstand rating or simply a casting penalty of the caster's Arcana, at some point in development, and something changed without fully propagating throughout the system texts. (Peep at Dispel Magic to see some of that.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T02:45:54-08:00","id":1004310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996316-clash-of-wills?p=996447#post996447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless specified, you usually cannot spend WP if you're unaware, no.<br /> <br /> As for Spell Cloak, there's no need for the attainment; remember, <i>all</i> concealment spells work automatically against Peripheral Mage Sight without a Clash. Only Active Sight provokes it. A Prime 2 Veiling spell cast either as a Combined spell or by an ally could cover it up pretty easily (with a ruling that, naturally, a spell that veils another spell also veils itself*).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">*Also, any Paradox caused by such a spell summons an Abyssal entity known as The One Who Shaves The Barber.</span><br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">This doesn't really ruin the intent of the defending spell, though. The Apprentice doesn't know if the Clash is caused by Alter Mental Pattern, or Mental Shield, or a Counterspell, or a Goetic demon surfacing or the Adept carrying a coin of thaumium... The list goes on. There is a huge list of reasons a spell might go pop off of someone.<br /> <br /> The rules aren't really clear whether he knows he wins the Clash or not. Presumably, all the Mage senses is that he gets an answer. It could be true, it could be false. Such is the paranoid world the Awakened live in.<br /> <br /> And even <i>if</i> they get the information back, do they know what patterns are being changed? By whom? To what end?<br /> <br /> So much information is not revealed still. Remember, all it says is that a Mage knows when their spells are clashing. It doesn't say they know the outcomes beyond what their other senses may tell them.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>The only problem with this is that if you intend upon hiding the existence of something and someone clashes, all they have to do is keep on trying. Eventually the person hiding whatever it is will lose. That's a HUGE gaping problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T03:14:40-08:00","id":1004317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996316-clash-of-wills?p=1004310#post1004310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only problem with this is that if you intend upon hiding the existence of something and someone clashes, all they have to do is keep on trying. Eventually the person hiding whatever it is will lose. That's a HUGE gaping problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Add a cumulative penalty for repeating a failed action. If you fail the first time you get another attempt to boost the right spell factors to increase your dice pool, but if you fail again you're already down to -2 on the roll, and has most likely gained a Paradox die and lost Mana due to extra Reaches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T03:31:06-08:00","id":1004320,"title":"","content":"Yeah, whenever a player fails an instant action roll I tell them they can do it again but will get -1 to the roll, and that's cumulative every time they fail on that action. They usually don't try any particular action more than twice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T04:47:07-08:00","id":1004333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996316-clash-of-wills?p=1004320#post1004320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, whenever a player fails an instant action roll I tell them they can do it again but will get -1 to the roll, and that's cumulative every time they fail on that action. They usually don't try any particular action more than twice.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the basis for it? Is it just gameplay balance, or do you have in game reasons for the houserule? The former is important, but the later is why we play (or, well, it at least is for me...sometimes).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T04:51:01-08:00","id":1004335,"title":"","content":"It keeps players from attempting to do the same thing more times than is interesting, and is simpler than slapping a Condition on them for a failed roll as happens with Extended Actions. If you want an insane reason, failure whittles away at your confidence that you can do it which reduces your effectiveness at doing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T07:10:50-08:00","id":1004391,"title":"","content":"Adding a cumulative -1 for repeating a failed action is a pretty old rule for CofD.<br /> <br /> As for another reason, it could just be that repeatedly defending against your attempts leaves the defender aware of your patterns.<br /> <br /> Truth be told, another houserule might simply be to say that you only get one shot at piercing it and, unless something changes, you can't get through it; the spell has successfully obfuscated you. Same reason you can't retry Revelation until you've Scrutinized a bit; there is simply a barrier there and you can't get around it.<br /> <br /> Another fun thing to do is to keep the result of the defender's roll hidden and tell them only what they see, if you want to enhance the uncertainty and paranoia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T17:18:22-08:00","id":1004714,"title":"","content":"CofD Core, page 72. Successive attempts. It's probably in the Mage book, too, but I don't feel like looking at it. The -1 thing is RAW, not a house rule or anything. If you're like me and care about that distinction. Though it only applies when there is &quot;pressure to perform.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T18:26:56-08:00","id":1004733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996316-clash-of-wills?p=1004714#post1004714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">CofD Core, page 72. Successive attempts. It's probably in the Mage book, too, but I don't feel like looking at it. The -1 thing is RAW, not a house rule or anything. If you're like me and care about that distinction. Though it only applies when there is &amp;quot;pressure to perform.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I don't have the core CofD book, so that's why I didn't know. Not a bad rule, though. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T11:13:46-08:00","id":1005034,"title":"","content":"<i>Mage: The Awakening, Second Edition</i> pp214 - bottom right (&quot;Permutaions: Successive Attempts&quot;)<br /> The RAW states this applies when time is short and not on extended actions, but yes, it's in there.<br /> <br /> Seems they forgot to except combat rolls... Heh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T12:32:42-08:00","id":1005062,"title":"","content":"Well, I mean. Trying again takes another action. You get one instant action per turn of combat. It's not really an exception that needs listed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T12:43:25-08:00","id":1005066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996316-clash-of-wills?p=1005062#post1005062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I mean. Trying again takes another action. You get one instant action per turn of combat. It's not really an exception that needs listed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think what the Nate is getting at is that combat is definitely a situation where there is pressure to perform, and the successive attempts rules don't specify that they don't apply to rolls in combat. By a strict technical reading of the rules, you should therefore get a cumulative -1 penalty to successive attempts to hit the same target in combat each time you miss. That's probably not the intent of the rule.<br /> <br /> But, what else is new. CofD is written in natural language, so technical readings produce weird results.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T12:50:51-08:00","id":1005068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996316-clash-of-wills?p=1005066#post1005066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> But, what else is new. CofD is written in natural language, so technical readings produce weird results.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reading CofD mechanics hyper-literally is just utter death, especially when the person mixes up their terms, or flat out gets something <i>wrong</i>. They always take their uncharitable (frequently incorrect) reading to the most absurd logical extreme, and then crow about how it's all broken.<br /> <br /> And it's, like, do they even play these games?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 11-18-2016, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}